From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 20:06:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] build: add a Qt4 build path to the cmake files

Qt4 is selected either with -DBUILD_WITH_QT4=ON or,as downstream
packagers have always done it,with -DQT5=0.

The Qt4 path uses FindQt4/UseQt4 and the QT4_WRAP_* macros instead of
AUTOMOC/AUTOUIC/AUTORCC,looks for QtDBus separately(it is only needed by
the internal lxqt_wallet kwallet-over-dbus backend) and locates the
QJson4 drop in replacement for Qt5's QJson* classes:

    https://github.com/eteran/qjson4

An external lxqt_wallet is never usable from a Qt4 binary so the
internal copy is forced on.  The build instructions document the option.

No source file is touched yet,this commit only adds the plumbing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J3PANPjHirYuwBkTemGj8R
